{"id":"a0adb8444eeba120","group":"89","path":"89/89-thm-settheoretic-completeness.md","title":"Set-Theoretic Completeness for I and J","display":"thm-settheoretic-completeness — Set-Theoretic Completeness for I and J","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-thm-settheoretic-completeness","aliases":["89-thm-settheoretic-completeness"],"display":"thm-settheoretic-completeness — Set-Theoretic Completeness for I and J","depends_on":["[[89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics]]","[[89-df-settheoretic-realization]]","[[89-df-finite-prewellorder]]","[[89-df-valid-modal]]"],"created":"2026-10-05","revised":"2026-10-05"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-thm-settheoretic-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-thm-settheoretic-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-settheoretic-completeness — Set-Theoretic Completeness for I and J"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0cb6343156d01ef0\" href=\"?note=0cb6343156d01ef0\" title=\"89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics\">89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"580b00b43dcd196a\" href=\"?note=580b00b43dcd196a\" title=\"89-df-settheoretic-realization\">89-df-settheoretic-realization</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ab51daf02675e633\" href=\"?note=ab51daf02675e633\" title=\"89-df-finite-prewellorder\">89-df-finite-prewellorder</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"dbba58e7bd3b0667\" href=\"?note=dbba58e7bd3b0667\" title=\"89-df-valid-modal\">89-df-valid-modal</a></span></div>"},{"key":"created","html":"2026-10-05"},{"key":"revised","html":"2026-10-05"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\">\\(A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\)</span>；所有 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r:\\mathrm{Prop}\\to\\mathrm{Sent}_{\\in}\">\\(r:\\mathrm{Prop}\\to\\mathrm{Sent}_{\\in}\\)</span> 取上述固定翻译。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>I 的算术式对应使用外部假设：存在无限多个序数 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_\\alpha\\models\\mathrm{ZF}+V=L\">\\(L_\\alpha\\models\\mathrm{ZF}+V=L\\)</span>。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>J 的对应使用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> 作为对象理论，并使用外部假设：存在无限多个强不可达基数。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZF}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZF}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}=\\mathrm{ZF}\\cup\\{\\mathrm{AC}\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}=\\mathrm{ZF}\\cup\\{\\mathrm{AC}\\}\\)</span> 及选择公理 AC 的约定取上述翻译原子。两个外部假设分别用于各自对应，不作为其对象理论新增公理。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm I,\\mathrm J\">\\(\\mathrm I,\\mathrm J\\)</span> 为上述定理集；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}\">\\(\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GLFrame}\">\\(\\mathrm{GLFrame}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}\\)</span> 为框架及有限性谓词；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}},\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}\">\\(\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}},\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}\\)</span> 为两种翻译，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{tm}\">\\(\\mathrm{tm}\\)</span> 为传递模型的上标。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}settheoretic\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\nA\\in\\mathrm I\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F\\\n(\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}(F)\\to F\\models A)\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZF}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}}(A)),\\\\\nA\\in\\mathrm J\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F=(W,R)\\\n\\bigl[(\\mathrm{GLFrame}(F)\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(W)\\land\n\\forall w,x\\in W(wRx\\lor w=x\\lor xRw))\\to F\\models A\\bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZFC}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}(A)).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}settheoretic\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\nA\\in\\mathrm I\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F\\\n(\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}(F)\\to F\\models A)\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZF}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}}(A)),\\\\\nA\\in\\mathrm J\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F=(W,R)\\\n\\bigl[(\\mathrm{GLFrame}(F)\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(W)\\land\n\\forall w,x\\in W(wRx\\lor w=x\\lor xRw))\\to F\\models A\\bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZFC}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}(A)).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Boolos, <em>The Logic of Provability</em>，第 13 章，印刷页 167–175；PDF 页码为印刷页加 39。本条采用本目录的等价语法约定。\nSolovay 的两项对应定理；原书分别用传递模型构造与不可达宇宙数目的分层句给出反解释，可靠性利用集合模型满足关系与相应绝对性。框架完全性本身不依赖大基数；显示的外部假设为完整集合论解释对应提供来源支持。原书 p.165 的选择公理约定用于 pp.173–175 的不可达宇宙定理，本条因此把其对象理论明确为 ZFC；I 的对象理论仍是 ZF。此条引用原书完整证明，未将集合论模型构造机械展开。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics","status":"resolved","id":"0cb6343156d01ef0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-settheoretic-realization","status":"resolved","id":"580b00b43dcd196a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-settheoretic-realization]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-finite-prewellorder","status":"resolved","id":"ab51daf02675e633","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-finite-prewellorder]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-valid-modal","status":"resolved","id":"dbba58e7bd3b0667","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-valid-modal]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}","display":false},{"tex":"r:\\mathrm{Prop}\\to\\mathrm{Sent}_{\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha","display":false},{"tex":"L_\\alpha\\models\\mathrm{ZF}+V=L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZF}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}=\\mathrm{ZF}\\cup\\{\\mathrm{AC}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm I,\\mathrm J","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GLFrame}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}},\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{tm}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}settheoretic\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\nA\\in\\mathrm I\n&\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F\\\n(\\mathrm{PreWO}_{\\mathrm{fin}}(F)\\to F\\models A)\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZF}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm{tm}}(A)),\\\\\nA\\in\\mathrm J\n&\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall F=(W,R)\\\n\\bigl[(\\mathrm{GLFrame}(F)\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(W)\\land\n\\forall w,x\\in W(wRx\\lor w=x\\lor xRw))\\to F\\models A\\bigr]\\\\\n&\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall r\\ (\\mathrm{ZFC}\\vdash\\tau_r^{\\mathrm u}(A)).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":2531,"backlinks":[{"id":"e0c421a5b45aeb77","anchor":"ref-148","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[89-df-finite-prewellorder]] → [[89-df-settheoretic-modal-logics]] → [[89-df-settheoretic-realization]] → [[89-thm-settheoretic-completeness]]"}],"outgoing":["0cb6343156d01ef0","580b00b43dcd196a","ab51daf02675e633","dbba58e7bd3b0667"]}